nction: an end that is a valid timestamp but not after start (RangeError) comes before the duplicate check (TypeError). My order handles this.\n\nAlso note: \"bookings must be an array\" — what if bookings is an array-like or a subclass of Array? Array.isArray covers subclasses. Non-array → TypeError.\n\nIf a booking element has a valid shape but `end` is fine and `start` is a real moment... all covered.\n\nNow let me sanity-check daysFromCivil against 1970-01-01:\ny=1970, m=1, d=1. m <= 2 so yy = 1969. era = floor(1969/400) = 4. yoe = 1969 - 1600 = 369. doy = floor((153*(1+9)+2)/5) + 1 - 1 = floor(1532/5) = 306. Wait: 153*10 = 1530, +2 = 1532, /5 = 306.4 → floor 306. doy = 306 + 0 = 306. doe = 369*365 + floor(369/4) - floor(369/100) + 306 = 134685 + 92 - 3 + 306 = 135080. days = 4*146097 + 135080 - 719468 = 584388 + 135080 - 719468 = 0. ✓\n\n2026-02-30: daysInMonth for February 2026: 2026 is not a leap year (2026%4 = 2) → 28. 30 > 28 → null → TypeError. ✓\n\nLeap year 2024: 2024%4=0, %100≠0 → leap → Feb 29 valid. ✓\nYear 1900: %100===0 and not %400 → not a leap → Feb 29 invalid. ✓\nYear 2000: %400===0 → leap. ✓\n\nYear \"0000\": y=0. isLeapYear(0): 0%4===0, 0%100===0, 0%400===0 → leap. daysFromCivil(0,1,1): yy=-1, era=floor(-1/400) = -1 (JS floor via Math.floor), yoe = -1 - (-400) = 399. doy for m=1: floor(153*10/5... wait (153*(1+9)+2)/5 = 306, doy=306+1-1=306. doe = 399*365 + floor(399/4) - floor(399/100) + 306 = 145635 + 99 - 3 + 306 = 146037. days = -146097 + 146037 - 719468 = -865528. Fine, numeric and consistent. No Date pitfalls. ✓\n\nTest 1: bookings b (09:00–10:00, R1), a (09:30–11:00, R1). Both valid, no dup ids. Overlap: same room, b.start (09:00) < a.end (11:00) and a.start (09:30) < b.end (10:00) → conflict. Pair: idA < idB → \"a\" < \"b\" → [\"a\",\"b\"]. ✓\n\nTest 2: different rooms → []. ✓\n\nMutation (R6): we only read. ✓\n\nLet me also think about whether the element check should be a TypeError — yes, per R1 (\"every booking needs...\"), so invali